Contact of an MPP v2 pen from the force tone of every position window (ForceToneContact)

iptsd decides the contact once per frame, in the pressure window: contact if there is a pressure
tone, else the MPP v2 flag of the 0x07 window, else the signal strength (ZeroForceContact). The
pressure tone outlasts the force by a frame, and the signal strength of a pen that is being
lifted stays high for a while, so strokes end late and strokes that follow each other closely
are joined. Measured on the Surface Pro 9 with the Slim Pen 2 against what Windows makes of the
same frames: contact ends 10 to 22 ms later (median), and 1 to 7 strokes per 8 s of handwriting
are missing because they were joined (12 strokes instead of 19 with a tilted pen).

The pen sends a tone in one of two rows of every position window, depending on whether its tip
switch is closed: rows 1 / 2 of the 0x06 window and rows 3 / 2 of the 0x07 and 0x08 windows.
With [DFT] ForceToneContact the contact is decided at each of the 0x07 and 0x08 windows:

 - Force: two windows in a row with the force tone, until two in a row without it.
 - Without force the tip signal decides (ZeroForceContact, ZeroForceEnter, ZeroForceExit and
   ZeroForceReference as before), but out of hover it has to stay above ZeroForceEnter for
   ZeroForceStartSamples samples.
 - ZeroForceStrokeLevel: a stroke that had force also ends when the tip signal falls below this
   share of what it was while there was force (a lifted pen loses a few percent of its signal
   long before it falls below ZeroForceExit).
 - ZeroForceLockoutPressure: when the force ends and one of the last three pressure windows was
   at or above this pressure, the pen was lifted on purpose: no zero force contact for
   ZeroForceLockoutSamples samples.

The eraser keeps the criterion of the pressure window. Off by default.

With 8 samples, 0.85, 0.22 and 50 samples, replayed captures against Windows (strokes in 8 to
12 s of handwriting, Windows / before / after): small light writing 53 / 47 / 50, normal 30 / 27
/ 31 and 30 / 29 / 31, tilted pen 19 / 12 / 19, light 21 / 19 / 21. Stroke ends are within -5 ..
+2 ms (median; +10 .. +22 before), starts within 0 ms (0 .. -30 before). No contact while
hovering at 5 mm. A pen resting on the glass without force is a steady contact.

